This is a greedy solution with a small local-search-free design: choose the order of libraries greedily, then assign books.

**Approach**
- Keep a `taken` flag for each book. At each step, evaluate every unused library with the current time `t` (the day its signup would start).
- If the signup finishes at `t+T`, the library has `D-t-T` days left, so it can ship `cap = (D-t-T)*M` books.
- Its value is the sum of the top `cap` scores among its untaken books. The ratio value/T is the selection key.
- Re-evaluating all libraries at every step costs O(L · N), which is too slow. Instead I use a lazy priority queue: the ratio only decreases as books get taken and as `t` grows, so a stale key is always an upper bound.
- Pop the top library, recompute its key with the current state, and if it is still at least the next top's key, accept it. Otherwise push it back with the new key.
- Computing a key needs the library's books sorted by score descending (presorted once). Scan them, skipping taken ones, until `cap` books are collected. This costs at most the library size per evaluation. Lazy re-evaluations are limited in practice. For safety, add a time check: if elapsed time exceeds about 8 s, accept the popped library with its fresh key without further comparison.
- Libraries with a non-positive key are skipped, and libraries with `t+T >= D` are skipped.
- When a library is accepted, mark its chosen books taken and output them. Chosen books are the top `cap` untaken ones, with K at least 1 and at most N.
- Monotonicity: the stale key is an upper bound, since `t` only grows (so `cap` shrinks) and taken books only reduce value. T is fixed, so the ratio is monotone.

**Output**
Buffer the output, since the count A is only known at the end. Each accepted library prints `Y K` followed by its books.

**Details**
- Sort each library's books by score descending, with ties broken by book ID for determinism.
- Store books in a flat array with offsets.
- `cap` may be huge (up to 1e10), so use `long long`.
- Key as a double: value/T.
- The priority queue holds (key, library ID), with ties broken by lower ID.

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main(){
    int B,L,D;
    scanf("%d %d %d",&B,&L,&D);
    vector<int> s(B);
    for(auto&x:s)scanf("%d",&x);
    vector<int> N(L),T(L),M(L),off(L+1,0);
    vector<int> flat;
    flat.reserve(1000000);
    for(int j=0;j<L;j++){
        scanf("%d %d %d",&N[j],&T[j],&M[j]);
        off[j]=flat.size();
        for(int i=0;i<N[j];i++){int b;scanf("%d",&b);flat.push_back(b);}
        sort(flat.begin()+off[j],flat.end(),[&](int a,int b){
            if(s[a]!=s[b])return s[a]>s[b];
            return a<b;});
    }
    off[L]=flat.size();
    vector<char> taken(B,0);
    long long t=0;
    auto eval=[&](int j)->double{
        long long left=(long long)D-t-T[j];
        if(left<=0)return -1;
        long long cap=left*M[j];
        long long cnt=0,val=0;
        for(int i=off[j];i<off[j+1]&&cnt<cap;i++){
            if(!taken[flat[i]]){val+=s[flat[i]];cnt++;}
        }
        return (double)val/T[j];
    };
    typedef pair<double,int> P;
    auto cmp=[](const P&a,const P&b){
        if(a.first!=b.first)return a.first<b.first;
        return a.second>b.second;};
    priority_queue<P,vector<P>,decltype(cmp)> pq(cmp);
    for(int j=0;j<L;j++){
        double k=eval(j);
        if(k>0)pq.push({k,j});
    }
    auto st=chrono::steady_clock::now();
    string out;
    int A=0;
    while(!pq.empty()){
        P p=pq.top();pq.pop();
        int j=p.second;
        double k=eval(j);
        if(k<=0)continue;
        bool late=chrono::duration<double>(chrono::steady_clock::now()-st).count()>7.5;
        if(!late&&!pq.empty()){
            P q=pq.top();
            if(cmp(P(k,j),q)){
                pq.push({k,j});
                continue;
            }
        }
        long long left=(long long)D-t-T[j];
        long long cap=left*M[j];
        vector<int> ch;
        for(int i=off[j];i<off[j+1]&&(long long)ch.size()<cap;i++){
            if(!taken[flat[i]]){ch.push_back(flat[i]);}
        }
        if(ch.empty())continue;
        for(int b:ch)taken[b]=1;
        A++;
        out+=to_string(j)+" "+to_string(ch.size())+"\n";
        for(size_t i=0;i<ch.size();i++){
            out+=to_string(ch[i]);
            out+=(i+1<ch.size()?' ':'\n');
        }
        t+=T[j];
    }
    printf("%d\n",A);
    fputs(out.c_str(),stdout);
}
```
